    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="1006" n="994" xml:id="pg994"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A Pacific War/502: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-12">June 12,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received June 13—3:46 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3551. American interests Far East. Department’s 1023, April 30.<anchor n="71"
                        xml:id="d867-f1"/> Swiss Legation, Tokyo, reports no requests received
                    financial assistance American POW interned Japan and Japanese occupied
                    territories. Believes this attributable poor provisioning camp canteens and sale
                    only cheap articles. However, Swiss Legation endeavoring ascertain whether and
                    how financial assistance may be accorded American POW Far East.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d867-f1" n="71" xml:id="d867-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it inquired if salaries were being paid to American officer
                    prisoners of war in Formosa, Malaya, the Philippines, and Java and if the Swiss
                    were making payments of pocket money to American prisoners of war in any of
                    these districts (740.00114A Pacific War/421a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
